Report the caller address the Secure Engine interface checks.

DIAGNOSTIC PATCH, off unless -DPORT_SE_CRYPTO_TRACE is passed
(CRYPTO_TRACE=1 in the Makefile).  It adds printf calls and changes no
logic.

__IS_SFU_RESERVED() returns a bare SE_ERROR when the caller's LR is outside
the SBSFU ROM region, without setting the SE_StatusTypeDef and without
reaching the call gate.  That is precisely what was observed here: ST's
verify loop gets SE_ERROR from SE_Decrypt_Append, the gate's own trace
(patches/0004-*) shows the gate is never entered, and the identical call
from main() succeeds.  The check is about WHERE THE CALLER IS, and nothing
else in the system reports that, so it is printed here.

